{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"alias":"jadeite-circular-roadrunner","creation_channel":"cli","description":"## Context\nDuring the comment-remediation epic, Gerrit briefly advertised `main` with parent `0fe2cc2e…` while Gitiles returned 404 for that object. Ref history appeared rewound and omitted merged commit `2a93f180…`. `git fetch gerrit main` returned timeout/HTTP 504, and CI run `34235734839` failed checkout when Gerrit returned HTTP 502 fetching change 2834. The service later recovered: the parent became readable and ref advertisement worked again.\n\nA separate `/rebar-debug` session owns investigation. This ticket records the incident only; the comment-remediation epic must continue without debugging Gerrit here.\n\n## Plan\n- Reconstruct the Gerrit ref and object-availability timeline from durable server and CI evidence.\n- Determine why an advertised parent was temporarily unreadable and why checkout/fetch returned 502/504.\n- Prove the root cause before proposing a fix, following `/rebar-debug`.\n- Add regression or operational safeguards appropriate to the confirmed failure class.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] The incident timeline is supported by exact Gerrit and CI evidence.\n- [ ] A reproducible or otherwise proven root cause explains the ref/object inconsistency and 502/504 responses.\n- [ ] The failure-class remediation is implemented or a concrete operator runbook is documented.\n- [ ] Verification evidence demonstrates the remediation.","id":"93e5-b934-b2ec-43d2","parent_id":"","priority":1,"tags":["gerrit","infra","debug"],"ticket_type":"bug","title":"Investigate transient Gerrit ref inconsistency and checkout 502"},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"CREATE","timestamp":1788892467914096001,"uuid":"4d251eae-c060-492d-aa52-0b59e4ed9802"}